> API and interpretation

All row counts and neighbor IDs are checked before traversal; negative counts
fail and the empty graph is valid. Self loops and duplicate directed entries are
retained and counted. Actual low-link arrays and component IDs come from the
producing kernel. Capture does not run a second SCC traversal.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Tarjan, Depth-First Search and Linear Graph Algorithms, SIAM Journal on Computing1 (1972),146-160|https://doi.org/10.1137/0201010]

